{"FixedQueuePool.shutdown tries q.shutdown(immediate=False) but queue.Queue has no shutdown method, will raise AttributeError": 0.8735030293464661, "OrderedQueueWorker.run uses work_queue.get() with no timeout which combined with missing shutdown API can hang on shutdown": 0.9047869443893433, "Workers will block forever on queue.get() on shutdown since there's no proper shutdown signaling mechanism": 0.9409141540527344, "FixedQueuePool.shutdown sets worker.shutdown=True but workers blocked on get() won't see it, leading to hang": 0.9377843737602234, "OrderedQueueWorker.result_processor signature/typing is brittle - should document that ResultProcessor must be callable with (identifier, result) signature": 0.08227867633104324, "Potential minor race condition in OffsetTracker._get_partition_lock if two threads try to create a lock for same partition concurrently": 0.6366379857063293, "work_queue.put is unbounded (queue.Queue() default is infinite) but docstring mentions 'Natural backpressure when queues fill up' - consider bounding the queue with Queue(maxsize=...)": 0.2818881869316101, "Missing worker_id tag in queue depth gauge metrics - only identifier tag is passed, adding worker_id would help debugging imbalances": 0.07455381006002426, "OrderedQueueWorker.run finally block calls complete_offset using work_item.partition/offset but work_item may not be set if get raises - need to wrap finally to only call complete_offset when work_item was retrieved": 0.24510416388511658, "Missing unit test verifying shutdown does not hang": 0.18841767311096191, "Test for graceful shutdown may get exception before clearing queue_pool because q.shutdown() raises": 0.8614569902420044}